Record every current finding as accepted, so later scans report only new ones

Usage: siloscan baseline [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]
          Path to scan

          [default: .]

Options:
      --rules <DIR>
          Rule directories

      --no-default-rules
          Do not load the built-in rule pack (a run that ends up with no rules at all checks nothing and is refused with exit 2)

      --config <FILE>
          Repository config (defaults to the nearest `siloscan.toml` at PATH, or above it only when a `.git` marker exists at or above PATH; pass this explicitly for an exported tree that has none)

      --coverage-report <FILE>
          Coverage report to feed coverage rules (lcov or cobertura); required when any coverage rule is loaded, since a gate with no input reports nothing and would read as a pass

      --follow-symlinks
          Follow symlinks whose target is inside the scan root; targets outside it are never followed

          A baseline records what a scan found, so this has to be available here and has to mean the same thing: a baseline taken with it off does not cover the findings a scan with it on will report.

      --no-cache
          Do not read or write the scan cache

      --cache-dir <DIR>
          Read and write cache entries under DIR instead of this user's cache directory

      --no-ignore
          Scan every file: ignore no `.gitignore` and no `.ignore`

      --no-gitignore
          Ignore `.ignore` files but not `.gitignore` files

      --respect-parent-ignores
          Also honor ignore files in directories above the scan root

      --respect-git-exclude
          Also honor `<PATH>/.git/info/exclude`

      --respect-global-gitignore
          Also honor git's global `core.excludesFile`

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
